        "id": 80520,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T17:33:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Copy and Paste since Matchstick is correct that this discussion should stay in this thread:</p><div><b>Matchstickman wrote:</b><blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p><b>Foote wrote:</b><br><blockquote>This certainly clears up the Pillars/Mistbound question from the other thread. Player choice.<p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Really? Because they are both start of turn effects so I was thinking the exact opposite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote></div><p>The point is that the interaction is \"ambiguous\" at best. The proof for that is that the thread was created at all and generated debated discussion. Sounds like all \"ambiguous\" situations fall under this new ruling. &nbsp;</p><p>\"Until\" vs \"At\" sounds a whole lot like \"dealt damage\" vs \"would be dealt damage\" debate (its all a timing issue). If Fort/SHD is coming down on the side of player choice, then this will as well.</p><p>You are free to argue that this situation is not, in fact, ambiguous at all. But I think this thread disagrees with that notion.</p><p>Edit: I would still play it at my table that these cards follow the simultaneous action rule and be resolved in card order. But I think the Order of Operations ruling leaves that choice to the players.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:02:40.903Z",
