      {
        "id": 80523,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T18:35:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The point is that the interaction is \"ambiguous\" at best. The proof for that is that the thread was created at all and generated debated discussion. Sounds like all \"ambiguous\" situations fall under this new ruling.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's… not what the ruling says.</p>\n<p>It says if it is a start of turn or end of turn effect it is resolved in card play order, if the cards do not refer to start of/end of turn and the situation is ambiguous then it falls to player choice.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jagarciao\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/48/2010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jagarciao:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But I don't think an effect that remains in place \"until the start of your next turn\" is considered a start of turn effect</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Then this ruling has no bearing on it.</p>\n<p>Either it is a start of turn effect and processed in card order or it is not a start of turn effect and we need further guidance on which 'phase' it actually expires.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;Would Mistbound stay in play for an entire round while it's effect is active?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>No. The effect remains but the card is removed. Just like damaging someone removes their HP and that effect remains even after the one-shot leaves play. Or Hypersonic Assault's \"no damage\" remains around.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:02:41.161Z",
