      {
        "id": 80524,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T18:53:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Foote wrote:</b><br><blockquote>The point is that the interaction is \"ambiguous\" at best. The proof for that is that the thread was created at all and generated debated discussion. Sounds like all \"ambiguous\" situations fall under this new ruling.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThat's... not what the ruling says.It says if it is a start of turn or end of turn effect it is resolved in card play order, if the cards do not refer to start of/end of turn and the situation is ambiguous then it falls to player choice.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Its not a start of turn effect in a traditional sense though (like Forced Deployment). Its an effect that activated a round ago and is persisting until a certain point.</p>\n<p>It is still reasonably ambiguous whether or not \"until the start of your turn\" includes the actual start of your turn. Again, if it was clear, there wouldn't be a thread about it. If its not clear, then it is an ambiguous interaction, which sounds like it defers to player choice.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:02:41.259Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
