      {
        "id": 80528,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T21:57:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Start of turn is as much a phase of a turn as Play, Power, or Draw. I'm not sure there's much disagreement on this point, but someone above seemed to be arguing that 'Start of turn' was just a point of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think the correct interpretation is that 'until the start ...' means that the effect ends just before the Start of turn phase.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, apologies for not adding much to the discussion besides weighing in on a particular side.</p>",
