      {
        "id": 80530,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-05T00:38:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p>I think the correct interpretation is that 'until the start ...' means that the effect ends just before the Start of turn phase.</p></blockquote><p>If someone said \"I'll wait for you until 2pm\", they don't mean they're going to leave at 1:59pm, they mean that they will wait until 2pm clicks over and then they will leave.&nbsp; I think that if you're doing something \"until the start of your turn\", the start of your turn (the trigger to end the until-loop) has to actually occur before the \"until-ed\" thing will end.</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:02:41.736Z",
